          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"dumas-fils-la-dame-aux-camelias-1aa634efc234\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.95,\"analysis\":\"The embedded proposition “je vous aime” is presented as a fact about the speaker’s continuing emotional state and as something the addressee should remember. It reassures and helps persuade him to accept her proposed arrangement, but it does not itself undertake a commitment. Despite the surrounding emotional language, there is no positive evidence that the words are a reflex-like expressive discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The declaration has relational and persuasive consequences, but these do not provide substantial independent support for performative undertaking force.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"A love avowal spoken directly by the woman to the narrator, syntactically embedded in the imperative “rappelez-vous seulement que je vous aime.”\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"The speaker is reasoning with and reassuring her interlocutor while proposing that they spend several months together in the country. She repeatedly presents her love as genuine—“mon amour pour vous” and “j'ai la folie de vous aimer”—and asks him to rely on it rather than worry. This makes the target primarily a deliberate avowal used persuasively, not an independently reflexive outburst or a commitment enacted by the words themselves.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"local-1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“rappelez-vous seulement que je vous aime, et ne vous inquiétez de rien”\",\"supports\":\"The complement “je vous aime” presents her continuing love as true and supplies reassurance, strongly supporting T.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"local-2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“j'ai trouvé le moyen de tout concilier, mes affaires et mon amour pour vous”\",\"supports\":\"She explicitly treats her love as an existing emotional state within a reasoned explanation, reinforcing T rather than reflexive E.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"local-3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“oui, pour vous, ne riez pas, j'ai la folie de vous aimer!”\",\"supports\":\"The nearby emphatic avowal corroborates the claimed loving state, but its intensity alone does not establish expressive/reflexive core force for the target occurrence.\",\"confidence\":0.94},{\"evidence_id\":\"local-4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Voyons, raisonnons un peu” and “Est-ce convenu, voyons?” frame the speech as reasoned persuasion toward agreement.\",\"supports\":\"The calculated argumentative framing weighs against treating the target as a reflex-like discharge; the requested agreement concerns the proposed country stay rather than a commitment enacted by “je vous aime.”\",\"confidence\":0.95}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core avowal. Its persuasive and reassuring use belongs to context and does not require P, E, or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":\"The exclamation in the preceding “j'ai la folie de vous aimer!” does not transfer expressive/reflexive force to the separately highlighted embedded occurrence.\"}"
        }
